This module formalizes Theory 4.3 (T3.3) from the provided context, proving that decomposition and specification form an adjunction between the lattice of function decompositions and the lattice of test suites.

Key definitions and theorems:
- `compose`: Defines the composition of test suites from components.
- `project`: Defines the projection of a product test suite into component test suites.
- `killedSet_decomposition_under_correctness`: Proves that the killed set of a product program decomposes into the union of the injected killed sets of its components, assuming component correctness.
- `killedSet_compose_decomposition`: Proves that the killed set of a composed test suite decomposes similarly.
- `T3_3_decomposition_specification_adjoint`: The main theorem establishing the Galois connection (adjunction) between decomposition (refinement of function structure) and specification (refinement of test suites). Specifically, `refines P T (compose T1 T2)` iff `refines P1 (project T).1 T1` and `refines P2 (project T).2 T2`.
